A||N||14||stimpy||Tinted windows- ooooooh!||||10||
Z||000000||stimpy||04-29-2000||01:07 PM||||<BR>Just got back from getting my windows tinted.  I've tried doing this myself before with the kit from Grand Auto, and believe me, it's worth the $150 to get it done professionally with a lifetime warranty! It looks oh so cool on my gold GT.  I have a couple of questions however.<BR>First, the dark tint on the side windows looks good, but it also shows off the scratches in the passenger side window. I guess my supple and smooth dew wipes are replacements by a former owner.<BR>Is there any glass polish that is bett than another for removing the majority of the minor scratches? Is it ok to use an orbital buffer on the glass?<BR>Second issue, my sail panels are destined to be replaced shortly after I get off my butt and call fieroshop to order them. Is it ok to tint these with film? George, do these come tinted? I mean, DARK tint?  <BR>Hope to get pics soon, let y'all know! I love living in the sunbelt where we don't have ridiculous laws banning tint on side windows!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||04-29-2000||01:23 PM||||I know about that Grand Auto stuff, You did the right thing. My son had his done (by the pros) It looked so good I gave him the keys to the little black toy and a little money<BR>(he had to pay the rest) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and told him to have mine done. I got a lot of remarks about it at your dad's car show. At night the back window looks like it is painted black. The sides or not as dark ....Cali law ya know?<BR>Black car Blacked out windows, looks dang good!<P>Yes Stimpy I also have the scratches I was just waiting to get new windows. The ones in the 87 coupe were in like new condition, as there was broken glass under the driver seat i'm sure that one was replaced. Was going to trade, but the Code 21 is gone.<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||04-29-2000||02:20 PM||||Answered my own question on one of my problems.  I used rain-x formula 2000 glass polish on my problem window.  It did take out the small scratches.  There are some deeper ones that I guess I'll learn to live with. If anyone knows of something that will work better, please let me know. BTW, this stuff also works great on chrome. Tomorrow if the rain doesn't come I am going to the coin-op for some serious detail time. Fiero Club of Oklahoma car show only 21 days away! <P>And for all you folks who haven't had the pleasure of seeing the DXR black beauty, the pics just don't do it justice! DXR_DAD is a CLEAN FREAK! Gotta be one of the nicest notchbacks I've seen. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||04-29-2000||04:31 PM||||I had my old 86 SE (silver/black) windows tinted. This was back in 1989 or so before the law started cracking down on the dark windows, atleast in Louisiana. I had mine done 5% all around and it was Dark! Looked good too. All those big trucks didn't blind me through the rear window at night anymore either.<BR>Thinking about getting my Coupe done now.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Loki||04-29-2000||04:46 PM||||They thing ive used for polishig galss or plastics. Is, well..Toothpaste.  Works wonders.. No particualr brand, just a gritty one. I usually use crest.....Dont laugh..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  give it a try.. Just take a finger and run away.||||reg||1
Z||000005||phillip||04-29-2000||07:59 PM||||5% on the back, sides, about an 9" band on the winshield top and 5" band on the bottom thats 5% too. import boyish? maybe. illegal? definitly, but the police can only cite you if they stop you for something else. a black paint job will set it off. if i get any where with the indy i may try white or mirror tint with the same layout.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DXR_DAD||04-29-2000||08:39 PM||||Thanks Stimpy, I've worked on cars for some time now, started with a 68 fierbird 400 in 1977 the first car I owned <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> The Fiero is a little different but with the help of this fourm I've made the adjustment. and love it!<P>And for those of you that don't know the Bay Area we are neck and neck with So. Cali. when it comes to street rods & custom cars so there is a lot of help out here. Most of the shops and people are Fiero friendly, so I don't get over charged or ripped off. Most of the work I do myself, I do have the DXR family to help also, we just love car, cars of any kind. I just haven't had a Low Rider......?  But..........naa I don't think so.||||reg||1
Z||000007||stimpy||04-29-2000||08:56 PM||||Naah? I figured a 71 Riviera would be proper for the DXR "treatment". I'm noy sayin 13x5 and little whitewalls, but 16x10 120 spoke knock-offs and a big bad 455? Think about it Bill. Juice it with a four-way dump. Hard to steal a car when the frame is sitting on the ground! Give all dem Impalas a dose of boattail and tiresmoke! ||||reg||1
Z||000008||AL||04-30-2000||01:31 AM||||hey dad, you may be close but so calif, is still the place to be for cars, no offense but it all started here! so have you found your gt yet? we seem to have a good supply of fiero's down here,if you want i'll keep an eye out for you? ||||reg||6
Z||000009||fieroshop||04-30-2000||02:53 AM||||Hey stimpy, the quarter glass does not come tinted, but you can always do that before you install. Just make sure that you do not have any tint where the tape goes or the windows will go flying. I know I the best price for GT quarter windows but even at $85.00 ea that's still a lot of money.||||reg||1
Z||000010||stimpy||04-30-2000||08:25 AM||||George. do your windows have a raised matrix patten around the edges like on the rear window glass? Window tint don't like to apply over that stuff either. <BR>Now I went and looked at the pics that Oreif posted in the mall with the fiberglass scoops with the window in them. hmmmmm, choices.||||reg||1
Z||000011||DJRice||05-01-2000||09:14 AM||||Stimpy, Right on with the Rivera!  Those things are double tough.  ||||reg||1
Z||000012||007DOUG||05-01-2000||06:30 PM||||Here's a picture of my 86 SE.(I tried using PIP for image hosting, but keep getting a "run time error of 503" anyone know what this is?)<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/tintedse.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/tintedse.jpg</A> <P>All windows, and a strip at the top/bottom of windshiled are 5%. The center of the windshield is 20%. I tried 5% in the middle, but its impossible to drive at night. I did the tint myself, and its really easy. The key is to make a pattern, and to apply the tint in your garage away from the sun.. <P>Looks awesome, or as the kids today say "phat". I just wish the inspection sticker was black too. LOL.<P>As for legality......Doctor's excuse. Check your law books. WV law states you are exempt from tint laws with an optometrists note.<P>I have also tinted the rear windows of my 88 GT. It can be done, but you can only wash your car when its cold (engine). The steam coming from a hot engine will loosen the tint. <BR>||||reg||6
Z||000013||DaRkLoRD||05-01-2000||06:45 PM||||I want to get mirror tint.. any idea how much $$$ that is, and if it's legal?||||reg||1
Z||000014||Haze_Performance||05-01-2000||11:01 PM||||I just had my windows tinted also. My drivers side also has the scratches in it. It pi$$ed me off. Are the scratches on the inside or outside of the glass? Looks to be the inside...... Oh I put Limo (Very Dark) on the rear & Medium on the sides. It cost me a cool $100.00 even lifetime war.<p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 05-01-2000).]||||reg||1
